---
title: "Kiosk Middleware Access Control (kintai-v3: Route Protection)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_path: incoming request
    q_check_path --> q_kiosk: path starts with /kiosk
    q_check_path --> q_check_public: other paths
    q_kiosk --> q_get_token: extract token from query param
    q_get_token --> q_no_env: KIOSK_ACCESS_TOKEN env not set
    q_no_env --> [*]: return 500 'Kiosk is not configured'
    q_get_token --> q_compare: env token present
    q_compare --> q_invalid_token: token != kioskToken
    q_invalid_token --> [*]: redirect to /dashboard (hide kiosk existence)
    q_compare --> q_valid_token: token matches
    q_valid_token --> [*]: NextResponse.next() (allow access)
    q_check_public --> q_is_public: path starts with /login OR /auth/
    q_is_public --> q_supabase_session: public path
    q_supabase_session --> [*]: updateSession(request) (Supabase session refresh)
    q_check_public --> q_check_oauth: non-public path
    q_check_oauth --> q_read_cookies: read oauth_user_id and oauth_access_token cookies
    q_read_cookies --> q_has_oauth: both cookies present
    q_has_oauth --> [*]: NextResponse.next() (allow access)
    q_read_cookies --> q_no_oauth: missing cookies
    q_no_oauth --> [*]: redirect to /login

    note right of q_compare
        INV-001: Kiosk access uses static token in query parameter (not session-based)
        INV-002: Invalid kiosk token redirects to /dashboard to hide kiosk endpoint
        INV-003: Query parameters are cleared on redirect to prevent token leakage
    end note

    note right of q_check_oauth
        INV-004: OAuth session check relies on two cookies (oauth_user_id, oauth_access_token)
        INV-005: Cookie presence check only - no validation of cookie values
        INV-006: Supabase session update only runs for public paths (login, auth)
    end note
